  "reason": "The top-4 results (config_049: 0.725, config_009: 0.721, config_020: 0.715, config_013: 0.713) all use scvi_n200 + multiprofile + multimodal, and all four aggregation×fusion combinations for scvi_n200 + imagenet_vit_l have been exhausted. The only untested RNA encoder paired with the best image encoder (imagenet_vit_l), aggregation (transformer), and fusion (weighted) is pca_n2000 (config_018). With 2000 retained dimensions, PCA preserves substantial transcriptomic variance and may complement the image features in a way that differs from scvi_n200's learned latent space. This is the last experiment, so the goal is to either (a) discover a configuration that beats the current best of 0.725, or (b) confirm that scvi_n200 is essential to the top performance. No other untested configuration has a realistic path to exceeding 0.725: resnet50 variants underperform vit_l by 1–3%, singleprofile drops accuracy to ~0.54, and scgpt was clearly inferior (~0.52). Config_018 is the highest-expected-value remaining bet."
